# tools/g/glow_shape_capacity_witness.rish -- Glow cannot write two of the product's four public
# types, and the number that stops it was frozen before the product existed.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. This seat's own ladder rung on construction/ITINERARY.md reads *express the
# receipt facts and Tally bounds in the smallest Glow form already owned*. The smallest form Glow
# owns for a record is the multi-field `$:` shape, and it holds at most `max_fields` faces --
# NINE, declared in glow/rune_shape.rye. The receipt contract Keaton accepted on `20260913`
# declares `ReceiptOfferFact` with FIFTEEN fields and `LinengrowReceipt` with ELEVEN. So the rung
# as written cannot be walked, and the reason is one constant.
#
# WHERE THE NINE CAME FROM, read rather than guessed. It is a seated capacity freeze
# (active-designing/date/20260720/20260720-231857_closed-field-capacity-freeze-and-framework-next.md,
# and the row in context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md that records it), and its stated reason was sound on the
# day it was written: the ladder had walked pair, triple, quad, penta, hexa, hepta, octa, nona,
# each rung a copy of the last, and *another face name teaches no new nest law*. Nothing asked for
# a tenth face. The freeze names its own escape in the same breath -- further named shapes stay
# horizon *unless a dedicated capacity pin is opened* -- so the door was left standing.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG DOES NOT DO. It does not widen anything. The freeze reserves that for Keaton's
# word, and this seat's stop line sends a Glow language ruling back to him. What a lap may do is
# make the gap a measured fact rather than an impression, so the decision has arithmetic in front
# of it.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, and why each. The INSTRUMENT is gated and the GAP is not. Both halves must be
# read from their own files -- the ceiling out of the Glow source, the types out of the contract's
# own `## Public types` block -- and at least one type must parse, because a reader that silently
# parses zero types prints a flawless `types_over_capacity=0` about a page it never opened. The
# gap itself is reported: closing it is a decision no lap may take, and a gate that reds every
# ship for a ruling nobody can make is a gate somebody turns off. That is the same shape the
# published-double reading takes in .claude/rules/derived-spine.md, and for the same reason.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, by tools/fixtures/g/glow_shape_capacity_control.sh -- 44 behaviors on
# planted files in a throwaway pen, every refusal shown from both sides:
#
#   THE FIELD COUNT, which is the reading a careless hand gets wrong in the flattering direction:
#     a type whose fields wrap across three lines reads as THREE to a line counter, and three is
#     under every capacity, so the careless reading calls an inexpressible type expressible. That
#     mutation is planted and bites.
#   THE TWO FIELD FORMS the contract actually writes -- a comma-separated list, and a `name: Type`
#     line whose type may itself carry a comma. The pen found this one: the first draft split on
#     commas before trimming the colon, so `offer: map<a, b>` read as two fields. Both directions
#     are now legs.
#   THE BOUNDARY, proven on a type sitting at exactly nine: at-or-over rather than over would call
#     a shape Glow holds inexpressible.
#   THE CAPACITY IS READ FROM THE FILE, proven by raising the planted ceiling to sixteen and
#     watching every type become expressible and the verdict follow.
#   FIVE REFUSALS, each planted and then lifted -- an absent Glow source, a renamed ceiling, an
#     absent contract, a page carrying no Public types block, and a block parsing to no type.
#   AND THE LIVE LEG, the real tree read as it stands, because a control that only ever reads its
#     own pen proves nothing about the tree it ships in.
#
# WHAT IT LEAVES TO OTHERS. Whether each field's own AURA is one Glow admits, which no reader can
# derive from the contract because the page names field names rather than types. Read by hand on
# `20260916`: all fifteen of ReceiptOfferFact's fields map onto the four admitted auras, with
# `value_amount` needing `@u64` because the contract's ceiling of 9,000,000,000 stands above what
# `@u32` holds, and `product_digest` fitting `@ux` exactly at its 32 bytes. So the capacity is the
# only thing in the way.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/glow_shape_capacity_witness.rish

say "glow-shape-capacity: Language EN -- a ceiling is a claim, and this one is measured."
say "glow-shape-capacity: Style Gauge, Meter -- the gap is counted, never adjudicated."
say "glow-shape-capacity: Lens TAME -- refuse a partial read; prove each branch from both sides."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/glow_shape_capacity_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "glow-shape-capacity: the control must complete -- its own lines are printed above"

assert control.out contains "control_expected=44" else "glow-shape-capacity: the control counts its own legs, so a shrunken pen cannot read as a full one"
assert control.out contains "control_legs=44" else "glow-shape-capacity: a leg added or lost is a leg nobody heard"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "glow-shape-capacity: every behavior must be satisfied"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "glow-shape-capacity: the control must balance before it is believed"

# The field count, proven in both the forms the contract writes and against the reading that flatters.
assert control.out contains "a wrapped type counts every comma-separated field" else "glow-shape-capacity: a type wrapped across lines must count its fields"
assert control.out contains "a colon form counts one field per line" else "glow-shape-capacity: a name-colon-type line is one field"
assert control.out contains "a field whose type carries a comma still counts once" else "glow-shape-capacity: a comma inside a field type must not become a field"
assert control.out contains "and splitting a colon line on commas first bites" else "glow-shape-capacity: the order of the two forms must be proven"
assert control.out contains "the line-counting mutation bites" else "glow-shape-capacity: counting lines rather than fields must bite"
assert control.out contains "the boundary mutation bites on the type sitting exactly at capacity" else "glow-shape-capacity: at-or-over must be told from over"

# The capacity follows its file rather than a copy carried here.
assert control.out contains "a raised capacity is read from the file" else "glow-shape-capacity: the ceiling must be read, never spelled"
assert control.out contains "nothing stands over at sixteen" else "glow-shape-capacity: a wide enough capacity must read clean"
assert control.out contains "the verdict follows" else "glow-shape-capacity: the verdict must follow the capacity"

# Five refusals, each planted and then lifted, because a refusal shown once cannot be told from an
# instrument that always refuses.
assert control.out contains "an absent Glow source refuses" else "glow-shape-capacity: a missing ceiling source must refuse"
assert control.out contains "a renamed ceiling refuses" else "glow-shape-capacity: a renamed constant must refuse rather than guess"
assert control.out contains "an absent contract refuses" else "glow-shape-capacity: a missing contract must refuse"
assert control.out contains "a missing block refuses" else "glow-shape-capacity: a page with no Public types block must refuse"
assert control.out contains "a block with no type name refuses" else "glow-shape-capacity: parsing zero types must refuse rather than pass clean"
assert control.out contains "and the refusal lifts when the heading returns" else "glow-shape-capacity: every refusal must lift when its cause does"

assert control.out contains "the tree's contract parses to at least one type" else "glow-shape-capacity: the live leg must read the real tree"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/glow_shape_capacity_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "glow-shape-capacity: the reading must complete"

# THE GATE: the instrument answered. Both halves read from their own files, and the contract's
# block parsed to the four types it declares. A reader that silently parsed none would print a
# flawless zero about a page it never opened.
assert scan.out contains "glow_readable=yes" else "glow-shape-capacity: the Glow shape source must stand where the reading expects it"
assert scan.out contains "capacity_found=yes" else "glow-shape-capacity: the ceiling must be found rather than assumed"
assert scan.out contains "contract_readable=yes" else "glow-shape-capacity: the contract must stand where the reading expects it"
assert scan.out contains "types_block_found=yes" else "glow-shape-capacity: the Public types block must be found"
assert scan.out contains "types_read=4" else "glow-shape-capacity: the contract declares four public types"

# THE READING, reported rather than walled. These four lines are the arithmetic the capacity
# decision deserves in front of it, and every one of them moves the day either side moves: the
# ceiling when a capacity pin opens, the counts when the contract grows a type.
assert scan.out contains "shape_max_fields=9" else "glow-shape-capacity: the frozen capacity reads nine today"
assert scan.out contains "widest_type=ReceiptOfferFact" else "glow-shape-capacity: the widest public type is the receipt offer fact"
assert scan.out contains "widest_type_fields=15" else "glow-shape-capacity: the receipt offer fact names fifteen fields"
assert scan.out contains "types_over_capacity=2" else "glow-shape-capacity: two of the four public types stand above the capacity"
assert scan.out contains "capacity_gap=6" else "glow-shape-capacity: the gap is six faces"

say "glow-shape-capacity: GREEN -- capacity 9, widest public type 15, two of four inexpressible."
say "glow-shape-capacity: the gap is reported and gated nowhere; widening the freeze is Keaton's word."
